  }
  /* Scale, then position, then centre. The depth is a SCALE rather than a
     translateZ so each work's rendered height is known before it is placed —
     which is what makes a constant edge-to-edge gap possible at all. The
     -50% pair resolves against the unscaled box and is applied last, so the
     card's centre lands on --ty whatever the scale is. */
  .is-live .wcard {
    position: absolute;
    /* Capped on HEIGHT as well as width. Without the third term a 9:16
       stands 960px in a 900px viewport: it bleeds off the top and bottom
       of the screen at once, so its gap above and its gap below can never
       be seen together, and the pin's fade mask eats both ends. The cap is
       expressed as a width (height x aspect) so it can sit inside the same
